<% content_for :title, "Getting Started — Turf Totals" %>
<% content_for :meta_description, "Enter your first Turf Totals contest in about ten minutes: download Phantom, create your account, buy $25 of USDC with Apple Pay or a debit card, and play." %>

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-10 px-2 space-y-12">
  <header>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-heading mb-2">Getting Started</h1>
    <p class="text-secondary text-sm">
      Your first contest entry, start to finish, in about ten minutes &mdash; no crypto experience required.
    </p>
  </header>

  <%# At-a-glance overview of the five steps below. %>
  <section aria-label="Overview">
    <ol class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-3">
      <% [["1", "Get Phantom", "1 min"],
          ["2", "Create a wallet", "1 min"],
          ["3", "Create your account", "2 min"],
          ["4", "Buy $25 of USDC", "3 min"],
          ["5", "Enter a contest", "3 min"]].each do |number, label, minutes| %>
        <li class="card p-4 text-center space-y-1">
          <span class="mx-auto flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary font-bold"><%= number %></span>
          <p class="text-body font-semibold text-sm leading-tight"><%= label %></p>
          <p class="text-secondary text-xs"><%= minutes %></p>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-heading">Step 1 &mdash; Download Phantom</h2>
    <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
      Phantom is a free crypto wallet used by millions of people. It holds your money on your
      own device &mdash; not on our servers, and not on an exchange. You will use it twice:
      once to buy your entry money, and once to approve your contest entry.
    </p>
    <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
      Get it from the official site only:
      <a href="https://phantom.com/download" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-primary hover:underline">phantom.com/download</a>.
      Pick your browser &mdash; Chrome is shown below &mdash; and add the extension from the
      official listing. On a phone, the same page routes you to the App Store or Google Play,
      and every step below looks the same in the app.
    </p>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <%= render "pages/guide_figure",
            image: "01-download-phantom.png",
            alt: "Phantom download page with browser choices and Chrome highlighted",
            caption: "phantom.com/download — pick your browser" %>
      <%= render "pages/guide_figure",
            image: "02-add-to-chrome.png",
            alt: "Phantom on the Chrome Web Store with the Add to Chrome button highlighted",
            caption: "Add to Chrome from the official listing" %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-heading">Step 2 &mdash; Create a new wallet</h2>
    <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
      When the extension opens, choose <strong>Create a New Wallet</strong>, then
      <strong>Continue with Email</strong>. Your wallet is created from your email or
      Google/Apple account and stored securely across multiple factors &mdash; if you ever lose
      this computer, you recover it with that account and a 4-digit PIN. There are no seed
      phrases to copy down on this path, and nothing to lose.
    </p>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <%= render "pages/guide_figure",
            image: "03-create-new-wallet.png",
            alt: "Phantom setup screen with the Create a New Wallet button highlighted",
            caption: "Choose Create a New Wallet" %>
      <%= render "pages/guide_figure",
            image: "04-continue-with-email.png",
            alt: "Create a Wallet screen with the Continue with Email button highlighted",
            caption: "Continue with Email — the simplest setup" %>
    </div>
    <div class="card p-6 space-y-2">
      <p class="text-body font-semibold">Prefer the classic way?</p>
      <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Create a Recovery Phrase Wallet</strong> gives you a 12-word Secret Recovery
        Phrase instead. If you choose it: write the words on paper, never share them, and know
        they are the only backup &mdash; whoever has the words has the money.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-heading">Step 3 &mdash; Create your account</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-body space-y-2">
      <li>Set a <strong>strong password</strong> &mdash; it unlocks Phantom on this computer.</li>
      <li>Agree to the terms and press <strong>Continue</strong>.</li>
      <li>Pick a <strong>username</strong>, and you're good to go.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <%= render "pages/guide_figure",
            image: "05-create-password.png",
            alt: "Create a password screen with the terms checkbox and Continue button highlighted",
            caption: "Set a strong password and agree to the terms" %>
      <%= render "pages/guide_figure",
            image: "06-choose-username.png",
            alt: "Choose a username screen showing an available username",
            caption: "Pick a username" %>
      <%= render "pages/guide_figure",
            image: "07-good-to-go.png",
            alt: "Phantom confirmation screen reading You're good to go",
            caption: "That's the whole setup" %>
    </div>
    <div class="card p-6 space-y-3">
      <p class="text-body font-semibold">&#128273; Three safety rules</p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-body space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Download only from phantom.com/download.</strong> Ignore lookalikes and ads.</li>
        <li><strong>Your password, PIN, and recovery phrase are yours alone.</strong> Nobody legitimate will ever ask for them &mdash; not Phantom support, and never Turf Totals. Anyone who asks is a scammer.</li>
        <li><strong>Guard the email account behind your wallet.</strong> It can recover your wallet, so keep its own password strong and protected.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-heading">Step 4 &mdash; Buy $25 of USDC</h2>
    <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
      Contests are paid in <strong>USDC</strong>, a digital dollar: one USDC is worth one U.S. dollar,
      and it is backed one-for-one by real dollar reserves. You can buy it inside Phantom with
      Apple&nbsp;Pay or a debit card &mdash; no exchange account needed.
    </p>
    <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-body space-y-2">
      <li>In Phantom, choose <strong>Buy</strong>.</li>
      <li>Choose <strong>USDC</strong> (Phantom picks the Solana network for you &mdash; that is the right one).</li>
      <li>Enter <strong>$25</strong> &mdash; the minimum purchase &mdash; and select <strong>MoonPay</strong>.</li>
      <li>Pay with Apple&nbsp;Pay or your debit card. The USDC usually arrives in a minute or two.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
      Expect roughly <strong>$20 of USDC</strong> to arrive from a $25 purchase &mdash; the difference
      is MoonPay&rsquo;s card-processing fee, which goes to MoonPay, not to us. Twenty dollars covers a
      full contest entry, so one purchase is all you need to play. Your card statement will show
      the charge from MoonPay.
    </p>
    <div class="card p-6 space-y-2">
      <p class="text-body font-semibold">Already own crypto?</p>
      <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
        Skip MoonPay. Withdraw USDC from Coinbase, Kraken, or any exchange straight to your
        Phantom address &mdash; just be sure to choose the <strong>Solana network</strong> when you
        withdraw. Tap your wallet address at the top of Phantom to copy it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-heading">Step 5 &mdash; Sign in and enter a contest</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-body space-y-2">
      <li><%= link_to "Sign in", signin_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline" %> and choose <strong>Solana wallet</strong>.</li>
      <li>Approve the connection in Phantom, then approve the sign-in signature. The signature is free &mdash; it proves the wallet is yours and moves no money.</li>
      <li><%= link_to "Open a contest", root_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline" %> and make your six picks.</li>
      <li>Confirm the entry in Phantom. The approval screen shows the exact entry fee in USDC &mdash; that amount moves, and nothing else.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
      That last point is worth repeating: entering a contest is a single transfer of the exact
      entry fee. Turf Totals never asks for an open-ended spending approval, and your USDC stays
      in your own wallet until the moment you enter. You can verify every contest&rsquo;s funds on our
      <%= link_to "Proof of Reserves", proof_of_reserves_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline" %> page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-heading">Good questions</h2>
    <div class="space-y-5">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-heading">Why $25 when the entry is $19?</h3>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          $25 is MoonPay&rsquo;s minimum card purchase. Their processing fee takes roughly $5, and
          about $20 of USDC lands in your wallet &mdash; enough to cover a $19 entry.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-heading">Is connecting my wallet safe?</h3>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          Yes. Signing in is a free message signature, not a payment. Money moves only when you
          confirm a contest entry, and each entry moves exactly the fee shown &mdash; our
          <%= link_to "About page", about_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline" %> explains
          the on-chain design in detail.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-heading">How do I cash out?</h3>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          Winnings are paid in USDC straight to your wallet. From Phantom you can sell USDC back
          to your card through MoonPay, or send it to an exchange like Coinbase and withdraw to
          your bank.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-heading">What if I get stuck?</h3>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          Email <a href="mailto:alex@turfmonster.media" class="text-primary hover:underline">alex@turfmonster.media</a>
          and a human will help you through it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-6 space-y-2">
    <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
      Turf Totals is a skill-based game, and paid contests involve real money. Play with money
      you can afford to lose, and read our
      <%= link_to "Responsible Gaming", responsible_gaming_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline" %>
      and
      <%= link_to "State Eligibility", state_eligibility_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline" %>
      pages before you enter.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
